WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.099 --> 00:00:06.266
- Neon was hugely popular in
the ‘30s, ‘40s, the early ‘50s.

00:00:07.877 --> 00:00:10.120
With the advent of LED signs,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.203
a lot of the small neon shops folded.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:17.395
It's important to me to keep neon alive

00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:19.895
because I feel like there's so much

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:23.369
more that can be done with it.

00:00:31.785 --> 00:00:34.756
I'm Kirk Tunningley, and I'm a neon artist

00:00:34.756 --> 00:00:37.220
and a neon tube bender.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.574
I started doing neon, making
three dimensional sculptures

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.416
while I was in college, and now I've been

00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:47.558
working with neon for 38 years.

00:00:47.558 --> 00:00:50.299
In the Austin area, I'll probably have

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:53.632
75 or a 100 neon signs and I've probably

00:00:54.656 --> 00:00:57.573
made 500 or 600 signs in my career.

00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:08.241
Different signs take
different amounts of time.

00:01:08.241 --> 00:01:10.161
There are more elaborate signs where

00:01:10.161 --> 00:01:13.494
the glasswork could take 25 or 40 hours.

00:01:16.138 --> 00:01:19.883
To make a neon light, is a really simple process.

00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:23.179
There's two torches, one
is used to make curves

00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:26.512
and the other one, makes sharper angles.

00:01:27.718 --> 00:01:30.139
Each bend is heated up and brought

00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:32.859
to the pattern and formed and then

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.782
marked where your next bend is.

00:01:35.782 --> 00:01:38.219
When the glass is heated up, you cork off

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:40.659
one end of the glass tube
and then the other end,

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:44.126
I have a rubber hose and as you bend it,

00:01:44.126 --> 00:01:46.323
you blow into the glass to keep

00:01:46.323 --> 00:01:48.906
the inside of the tube uniform.

00:01:50.196 --> 00:01:54.363
It's a back and forth process
from torch to pattern.

00:01:56.376 --> 00:01:59.152
Something I really love about neon lights,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.985
it is the wild factor.

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:05.770
If you put up a display
even a simple display,

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.830
it excites people.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.997
There's nothing that looks
better than neon lights at night.

00:02:13.589 --> 00:02:15.552
I think it's important that people

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:18.802
keep up the tradition of bending glass.

